{"id":"R0239","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Evaluates multi-agent federated RL policy learning with onboard local execution rather than collaborative multi-UAV neural inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","present MulBERRY, a multi-agent robust learning framework","Primary research paper proposing a cross-layer multi-agent robust learning framework."],["E2","PDF",8,"6.1 System-Level UAV Experimental Setup","focus on a 4-UAV scenario for MulBERRY evaluation","Explicitly evaluates multi-UAV autonomous navigation swarms in PEDRA/AirSim."],["E3","PDF",14,"8 Related Work","MulBERRY targets learning as opposed to inference","Explicitly targets federated/multi-agent RL policy learning rather than collaborative inference."],["E3","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","with little-to-no offloading computation support","UAVs execute RL policies locally onboard without collaborative inference offloading."],["E4","PDF",8,"6.1 System-Level UAV Experimental Setup","build upon PEDRA, an open-source multi-UAV simulation infrastructure","Evaluated via multi-UAV simulation and hardware/thermal modeling in Sections 6-7."],["E5","PDF",1,"Copyright/Reference Strip","ASPLOS '24, April 27-May 1, 2024","2024 proceedings wholly within 2021-2026-11-26; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2024-04-27 could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","The use of autonomous Unmanned Aerial Vehicles","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-17."],["E7","https://www.asplos-conference.org/asplos2024/cfp/index.html",0,"Anonymizing","ASPLOS employs a double-blind review process","Official ASPLOS 2024 CFP confirms double-blind peer review for full conference papers."]]}
{"id":"R0240","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Evaluates federated learning training and aggregation of a detector rather than collaborative multi-UAV neural inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","we propose CMA-FL, a cognitive multi-agent assisted FL framework","Primary research report presenting a multi-agent federated learning framework."],["E2","PDF",2,"2 Problem Formulation","drone communication network with drone-edge clients","Models multiple drone-edge clients and evaluates simulated multi-client rounds in Section 4."],["E3","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","FL enables each drone-edge client to train","Federated learning training and server aggregation only; no collaborative inference distribution or placement."],["E4","PDF",4,"4 Results and Discussion","evaluate CMA-FL using a public drone communication dataset","Evaluated on an offline benchmark dataset against baselines in Section 4."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","October 26-30, 2026, Austin, TX","Cutoff-year 2026 event date on PDF; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2026-10-26 could not be re-opened to verify publication date."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","Drone communication is increasingly used for surveillance","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-6."],["E7","PDF",1,"Title","Poster: CMA-FL: Cognitive Multi-Agent Federated Learning","Six-page poster with method and benchmark results, but official DroneCom '26 poster-track peer-review policy could not be verified."]]}
{"id":"R0244","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluates a standalone centralized classifier on an offline dataset without any multi-UAV architecture or collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","proposes an attention-guided UAV intrusion detection framework","Primary research report proposing a feature-selection and attention-based classifier."],["E2","PDF",2,"3 Proposed Approach","use an existing dataset of UAV network traffic","Centralized offline dataset evaluation; no multi-UAV or swarm architecture is modeled or evaluated in Sections 3-4."],["E3","PDF",2,"3 Proposed Approach","consists of three stages: feature selection, feature refinement","Standalone single-model neural classification without distributed or collaborative inference across UAVs."],["E4","PDF",4,"4.1 Dataset Representation","tested the proposed intrusion detection framework on the UAVIDS-2025","Evaluated on UAVIDS-2025 with ablation and baseline comparisons in Section 4."],["E5","PDF",2,"Running Header","DroneCom '26, October 30, 2026, Austin","Cutoff-year 2026 event date on PDF; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2026-10-26 could not be re-opened to verify publication date."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) have become integral","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-6."],["E7","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","Proceedings of Drone-Assisted Wireless Communications for 5G","Six-page workshop paper with method and results, but official DroneCom '26 peer-review policy could not be verified."]]}
{"id":"R0245","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluates single-UAV standalone CNN+LSTM visual localization without multi-UAV architecture or collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","proposed a new approach based on LSTM","Primary research paper proposing a multi-height visual positioning method."],["E2","PDF",1,"Abstract","visual data captured by a UAV's onboard camera","Single-UAV visual localization evaluated in Sections 3-4; multi-UAV positioning is only mentioned in passing in Section 1."],["E3","PDF",3,"3.3 Solution","trained a CNN to extract features and then","Standalone single-drone CNN and LSTM inference without collaborative workload distribution."],["E4","PDF",4,"4.1 Training Process","use images of the entire Macau Peninsula","Evaluated on multi-height Macau Peninsula imagery against a single-height CNN baseline in Section 4."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ICCIP 2023, December 14-16, 2023, Lingshui, China","2023 proceedings wholly within 2021-2026-11-26; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2024-04-23 could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) have revolutionized various industries","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-6."],["E7","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","9th International Conference on Communication and Information Processing","Six-page conference paper with method and results, but 2023-edition ICCIP peer-review policy was not independently opened."]]}
{"id":"R0246","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluates a single UAV running non-DNN Radio Tomographic Imaging for radio environment mapping without multi-UAV or collaborative neural inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","develop SKYSCALE, a robust and scalable REM estimation","Primary research paper proposing an RTI-based REM estimation and UAV positioning system."],["E2","PDF",6,"4.1 UAV Implementation and Testbed Dataset","is a lightweight custom-built quadcopter with a flight","Evaluates a single custom-built UAV base station across testbed and trace experiments in Sections 4-5."],["E3","PDF",4,"3 Design of the SKYSCALE System","SKYSCALE uses an RTI based approach with improved","Uses Tikhonov-regularized RTI and watershed segmentation rather than collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",6,"4 UAV Testbed and Evaluation Datasets","evaluate SKYSCALE in an arena of size","Evaluated on WiFi UAV testbed, LTE traces, and Sionna 5G datasets in Sections 4-5."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","MobiHoc '24, October 14-17, 2024, Athens, Greece","2024 proceedings wholly within 2021-2026-11-26; Codex-supplied DOI 2024 metadata could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","Recently, Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV)-based platforms have emerged","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-10."],["E7","https://www.sigmobile.org/mobihoc/2024/cfp.html",0,"Call for Papers","highly selective single-track technical program","Official MobiHoc 2024 CFP confirms peer review with author rebuttal for full 10-page conference papers."]]}
{"id":"R0248","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Uses decentralized MADRL with Transformer strictly as a multi-UAV trajectory-planning optimizer for data collection without collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",6,"IV Proposed Solution","propose a decentralized MADRL method called","Primary research article proposing a decentralized MADRL trajectory-planning framework."],["E2","PDF",3,"III System Model","assume that a group of UAVs","Explicitly models and evaluates multiple UAVs across two urban crowdsensing datasets in Section V."],["E3","PDF",6,"IV-A Transformer-Enhanced Distributed MADRL Framework","follows decentralized training and decentralized execution (DTDE) paradigm","Neural network acts only as an independent trajectory optimizer without information sharing or collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",9,"V Experimental Results","utilize two real-world datasets containing taxi trajectories","Evaluated via trace-driven simulations against nine baselines plus ablation in Section V."],["E5","PDF",1,"First-page footnote","Date of publication 12 July 2023","IEEE first-publication date directly visible on PDF p. 1, wholly within 2021-2026-11-26 (current version 16 February 2024)."],["E6","PDF",1,"I Introduction","has become a promising paradigm to facilitate","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-16."],["E7","PDF",1,"First-page footnote","revised 22 May 2023; accepted 20 June 2023","Peer-reviewed IEEE/ACM Transactions on Networking journal article with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0249","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Models county-level post-disaster human population mobility recovery with a centralized Graph Neural ODE and evaluates no UAVs.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","propose a deep learning framework, named Coupled Dynamic","Primary research paper proposing a physics-informed Graph Neural ODE model."],["E2","PDF",6,"5.1.2 Dataset","records the daily number of people moving between","Evaluates county-level human mobility flows during Hurricane Dorian; no UAV setting is modeled or evaluated."],["E3","PDF",3,"4.1 Framework of Proposed Method","predict the population mobility recovery process post-disaster","Centralized Graph Neural ODE forecasting model; no multi-UAV collaborative inference."],["E4","PDF",6,"5.2 Performance Evaluation","assess the performance of different models in each","Evaluated on three state mobility datasets against six baselines plus ablation in Section 5."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","KDD '24, August 25-29, 2024, Barcelona, Spain","2024 proceedings wholly within 2021-2026-11-26; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2024-08-24 could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","The fast progress of urbanization and frequently occurred","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-12."],["E7","https://kdd.org/kdd2024/research-track-call-for-papers/",0,"Reviewing Process","Each submission will receive at least three independent reviews","Official KDD 2024 CFP confirms peer review for full 12-page conference papers."]]}
{"id":"R0251","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluates a single UAV with factor-graph sensor fusion and scheduling optimization rather than multi-UAV collaborative neural inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","proposes an integrated solution that integrates GNSS/INS/ vision","Primary research paper describing a UAV positioning, big data, and management system."],["E2","PDF",5,"6.2 Experimental Environment Setup","A DJI Matrice 300 RTK UAV is equipped","Evaluates a single UAV platform; Section 7.4 p. 6 explicitly notes multi-UAV swarm collaboration is not verified."],["E3","PDF",3,"3.1 Overall architecture of the model","takes the factor graph as the core framework","Uses factor-graph optimization, ORB/RANSAC, random forests, and DRL/GA scheduling; no collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",5,"6.3 Experimental Scenario Design","Three types of complex scenarios are designed","Evaluated across three operational scenarios reporting positioning, processing, and management metrics in Section 7."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ICCSMT 2025, December 26-28, 2025, Xiamen, China","PDF gives 2025 event/copyright year while Codex-supplied Crossref published-online is 2026-04 (month only, cutoff year) which could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","The rapid advancement of the digital economy","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-6."],["E7","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","6th International Conference on Computer Science and Management","Six-page proceedings paper with method and evaluation, but official ICCSMT 2025 peer-review policy could not be verified."]]}
{"id":"R0253","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Uses MADRL strictly as a decentralized UAV trajectory and crowdsensing task-allocation optimizer without collaborative DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",3,"1 Introduction","propose a dynamic hierarchical human-UAV cooperative task allocation","Primary research article proposing the Hi-HUTA hierarchical task allocation framework."],["E2","PDF",26,"5.10 A Case Study in Real Application Environment","we utilized five UAVs and recruited 20 volunteers","Explicitly evaluates multi-UAV settings in both simulations (Section 5.4) and a five-UAV campus case study."],["E3","PDF",10,"4.2 First layer","utilize MADRL-based method to decentralized learning optimal routes","MADRL actor-critic is used solely for UAV trajectory/task scheduling optimization; no collaborative DNN inference workload."],["E4","PDF",17,"5 Performance Evaluation","analyzes comparisons with seven baselines and SOTA methods","Evaluated via simulations against seven baselines, complexity analysis, and a real-world case study in Section 5."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Article 188. Publication date: December 2025.","Journal publication date December 2025 directly visible on PDF p. 1, wholly within 2021-2026-11-26; Codex-supplied Crossref 2025-12-02 could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","Mobile Crowdsensing (MCS) enables large-scale urban environmental data","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-33."],["E7","https://www.acm.org/publications/pacm/pacm-guidelines",0,"Criteria","Minimum of two expert reviewers with written reviews","Official ACM PACM guidelines confirm peer-reviewed journal status for IMWUT articles."]]}
{"id":"R0255","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Explicitly excludes multi-UAV operation from scope and evaluates strictly on-device standalone VLN inference on a single micro UAV.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","propose EdgeCurator, a 14.8M-parameter early-fusion framework","Primary research paper proposing an onboard cross-modal grounding architecture for UAV navigation."],["E2","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","Voice capture, multi-UAV operation, visitor comfort, manipulation","Explicitly places multi-UAV operation out of scope on physical p. 1."],["E2","PDF",2,"2.3 Embodied Agents in Interactive Spaces","do not evaluate speech recognition, visitor-facing interaction, or multi-UAV","Reconfirms multi-UAV operation is not evaluated; Section 4.1 p. 5 evaluates a single physical micro UAV."],["E3","PDF",7,"4.4.1 System Integration and Latency","The entire multimodal pipeline is strictly on-device","Standalone onboard inference on a single micro UAV without collaborative multi-UAV inference."],["E4","PDF",5,"4.1 Experimental Setup","deployed the trained policy on a physical micro UAV","Evaluated on the Expo-VLN simulation benchmark, ablations, and controlled physical micro-UAV trials in Section 4."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","EReL-MIR '26, November 10-14, 2026, Rio de Janeiro","Cutoff-month November 2026 event date on PDF; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2026-11-10 could not be re-opened to verify exact day."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","Efficient multimodal inference is difficult on aerial robots","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-9."],["E7","https://erel-mir.github.io/",0,"MM2026 Fast Track (new)","Such papers will bypass the peer-review process","Workshop offers both double-blind review and MM2026 Fast Track bypassing workshop review; exact track for this paper is not stated."]]}
{"id":"R0257","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluates split federated learning training on generic IoT edge clients using MNIST/Fashion-MNIST without any multi-UAV setting or collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",5,"1 Introduction","introduces GSFL, a novel FL algorithm that innovatively","Primary research article proposing a grouping-split federated learning algorithm."],["E2","PDF",20,"4.1.1 Dataset and Model","experiments employed datasets from Fashion-MNIST [45] and MNIST","Evaluates generic IoT/edge FL clients without any modeled or evaluated multi-UAV setting."],["E3","PDF",20,"3.2.3 Grouping FL Process Based on SL Mechanism","forward propagation on the local device-side group model","Split federated learning training (forward/backward passes and parameter aggregation in Algorithm 4), not collaborative inference."],["E4","PDF",22,"4.2 Experimental Results","GSFL algorithm demonstrates superior performance over FedAvg, HACCS","Evaluated on MNIST and Fashion-MNIST against four FL baselines in Section 4."],["E5","PDF",1,"Footer","Article 32. Publication date: November 2025.","Journal publication date November 2025 directly visible on PDF p. 1, wholly within 2021-2026-11-26; Codex-supplied Crossref 2025-11-26 could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","With the unceasing advancement of 5G technology","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-29."],["E7","PDF",29,"Article History","Received 20 February 2024; revised 6 November 2024","Peer-reviewed ACM TAAS journal article (accepted 14 March 2025) with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0259","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Runs a centralized LSTM energy-consumption predictor at the central station to guide UAV-BS deployment rather than collaborative multi-UAV neural inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1.0.2 Motivation and Contributions","proposes SemanticBlock, a blockchain-assisted framework that leverages semantic","Primary research paper proposing an energy-aware UAV-BS deployment and authentication framework."],["E2","PDF",4,"3 Performance Evaluation","samples collected from four UAVs at 5-minute intervals","Models multi-UAV units (Fig. 1 p. 3) and evaluates data from four UAVs and multi-UAV blockchain authentication."],["E3","PDF",2,"2 Proposed Architecture","oversees the execution of deep learning (DL) models","Central station executes a single LSTM predictor for UAV energy usage; no collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",4,"3 Performance Evaluation","conducted simulations using Google Collaboratory for deep learning","Evaluated via LSTM and blockchain simulations reporting metrics in Tables 1-2."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ICACS 2025, December 12-14, 2025, Bangkok, Thailand","PDF gives 2025 event/copyright year while Codex-supplied Crossref published-online is 2026-04-25 (cutoff year) which could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) have become a vital","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-6."],["E7","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","9th International Conference on Algorithms, Computing and Systems","Six-page proceedings paper with method and evaluation, but 2025-edition ICACS peer-review policy was not independently opened."]]}
{"id":"R0260","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Benchmarks single-device mobile/wearable versus cloudlet edge offload on smartphones and smartglasses with no UAVs evaluated.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","presents a set of end-to-end benchmarks for comparing","Primary research paper presenting computer vision benchmarks comparing on-device and edge-offloaded AI."],["E2","PDF",3,"3.3 Devices","investigate real-time AI performance on three mobile devices","Evaluates two smartphones and one smartglass with a cloudlet; drone swarm is mentioned only in passing in Section 1 p. 2."],["E3","PDF",4,"3.3 Devices","Mobile devices offload over WiFi to this cloudlet","Single-device on-device versus cloudlet offload benchmarking without multi-UAV collaborative inference."],["E4","PDF",4,"4.1 Experimental Setup","experiments use the well-known ImageNet-1K dataset","Evaluated experimentally across five computer vision tasks and energy measurements in Sections 4-9."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","SEC '25, December 3-6, 2025, Arlington, VA, USA","2025 proceedings wholly within 2021-2026-11-26; Codex-supplied Crossref published-online 2025-12-03 could not be re-opened."],["E6","PDF",1,"1 Introduction","As AI advances, so does its voracious appetite","Full text confirmed in English across physical pages 1-18."],["E7","https://acm-ieee-sec.org/2025/call_for_papers.php",0,"Submitting a Paper","The review process will be double-blind","Official SEC 2025 CFP confirms double-blind peer review (also corroborated by reviewer/shepherd acknowledgments on PDF p. 14)."]]}
